//! Trust: Verification MIR pass.
//!
//! Runs the Trust verification pipeline as a native MIR pass after optimization,
//! before codegen — inside the compiler rather than behind a driver callback, so
//! a verdict is bound to the same MIR codegen consumes.
//!
//! Pipeline: MIR Body -> trust-mir-extract -> trust_vcgen -> trust-router -> report
//!
//! The pass delegates to the trust-* crates for extraction and VC generation:
//!
//!   let func = trust_mir_extract::extract_function(tcx, body);
//!   let vcs = trust_vcgen::generate_vcs(&func);
//!
//! Verification is batteries-on. Raw `trustc`, its same-sysroot `rustc` alias,
//! and Cargo-authenticated primary crates use the strict native typed route by
//! default. `-Ztrust-verify=off` is the sole off-switch used by vanilla and
//! bootstrap lanes; survey mode (`-Ztrust-policy=advisory`) keeps verification
//! active nonfatally.
//!
//! What a passing verdict from this pass actually rests on — one row per
//! proof-authority class, and which of them the Clean kernel re-checks — is
//! `docs/TCB.md`, whose scope is this pass and everything upstream of it.
//!
// ignore-tidy-filelength
//! Author: Andrew Yates <andrewyates.name@gmail.com>
//! Copyright 2026 Andrew Yates | License: Apache 2.0

